9
00:31:09,230 --> 00:31:15,230
The DC Universe (DCU) is an American media franchise and shared
universe based on characters from DC Comics publications.

10
00:34:36,923 --> 00:34:42,923
It was created by James Gunn and Peter Safran,
co-chairmen and co-CEOs of DC Studios.

11
00:38:04,615 --> 00:38:10,615
The DCU is a soft reboot of a previous franchise, the DC Extended Universe (DCEU),
retaining select cast members and narrative elements but disregarding others.

12
00:41:32,307 --> 00:41:38,307
In contrast to the previous state of DC Comics adaptations, the DCU features a unified continuity
and story across live-action films and television, animation, and video games.

13
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Concurrent DC adaptations that do not fit this
continuity are labeled "DC Elseworlds".

14
00:48:27,692 --> 00:48:33,692
After Discovery, Inc.

15
00:51:55,384 --> 00:52:01,384
and WarnerMedia merged to become Warner Bros.

16
00:55:23,076 --> 00:55:29,076
Discovery (WBD), CEO David Zaslav revealed a plan to revitalize the
DC brand following the poor reception of the DCEU.

17
00:58:50,769 --> 00:58:56,769
Gunn and Safran were hired to lead the newly formed DC Studios in November 2022 after working on several DCEU
projects, including the film The Suicide Squad (2021) and its spin-off series Peacemaker (2022–2025).

18
01:02:18,461 --> 01:02:24,461
The pair spent several months with a group of writers developing the overarching story for a
new DC continuity that features a mix of popular and obscure DC characters.

19
01:05:46,153 --> 01:05:52,153
Some DCEU projects in development were abandoned in favor of new takes, while
others—including Peacemaker—continued within the new franchise.

20
01:09:13,846 --> 01:09:19,846
Certain DCEU actors reprise their roles in the DCU, with others recast.

21
01:12:41,538 --> 01:12:47,538
Gunn and Safran wanted to focus on storytelling needs rather than forcing
creators to complete their projects to meet specific release dates.

22
01:16:09,230 --> 01:16:15,230
The story of the DCU is divided into chapters.

23
01:19:36,923 --> 01:19:42,923
The first chapter, "Gods and Monsters", begins with the first season of
the animated series Creature Commandos, released in 2024.

24
01:23:04,615 --> 01:23:10,615
Gunn and Safran consider the chapter's first film, Superman
(2025), to be the true beginning of the DCU.

25
01:26:32,307 --> 01:26:38,307
The tone is intense.
